---
title: Diagrama de clases INICIAL (tag pre-refactor)
---
classDiagram
    direction LR

    class BaseModel {
        <<pydantic>>
    }
    class HTTPException {
        <<fastapi>>
        +status_code
        +detail
    }

    class Database {
        +path : str
        +connect() Connection
        +initialize() void
    }

    class ItemInput {
        +product_id : int
        +quantity : int
    }
    class OrderInput {
        +customer_id : int
        +address : str
        +city : str
        +postal_code : str
        +shipping : Literal
        +items : list~ItemInput~
        +unique_products() OrderInput
    }
    class ProductInput {
        +name : str
        +price_cents : int
        +stock : int
    }
    class CustomerInput {
        +name : str
        +email : EmailStr
        +category : Literal
    }

    class OrderService {
        +database : Database
        +save(customer_id, address, city, postal_code, shipping, items, order_id) dict
        +quote(data) dict
        +get(order_id) dict
        +list() list
        +confirm(order_id) dict
        +cancel(order_id) dict
        +delete(order_id) void
        +notifications(order_id) list
    }

    BaseModel <|-- ItemInput
    BaseModel <|-- OrderInput
    BaseModel <|-- ProductInput
    BaseModel <|-- CustomerInput
    OrderInput "1" *-- "1..*" ItemInput : items
    OrderService --> Database : usa
    OrderService ..> OrderInput : quote(data)
    OrderService ..> ItemInput : save(items)
    OrderService ..> HTTPException : lanza 404/409

    note for OrderService "Mezcla reglas de precio (descuento y envio duplicados en save y quote), SQL, transiciones de estado y notificaciones. Las rutas de products.py y customers.py (funciones, no clases) ejecutan SQL directamente sobre Database."
